Release Notes - SABnzbd 5.2.0 Release Candidate 2
=========================================================

This is the second release candidate of version 5.2.0, containing several major
improvements to the core download and post-processing handling.
Additionally, several vulnerabilities were fixed. This also required extra
restrictions and the removal of some functionality for security reasons.

## New features in 5.2.0

* Downloaded data will be written directly to disk (if your hardware supports it),
  which greatly reduces memory and CPU usage on systems with SSDs.
  Additionally, several other download performance improvements were made.
* par2cmdline is now incorporated in SABnzbd, resulting in several improvements:
    * Files are checked against par2 while they download, so verification
      no longer has to read them back from disk.
    * Damaged files are repaired in place instead of writing a repaired copy.
    * Multi-threading and memory usage are directly controlled by user limits.
    * Improved support for Unicode filenames.
* Search your indexers and add downloads directly from within SABnzbd.
* Post-Processing, Pre-Queue and Notification Scripts no longer receive
  command-line arguments. Use the `SAB_*` environment variables instead.
  This prevents attackers from easily gaining remote code execution.
* Download directories can no longer be inside the program directory.
  This also prevents attackers from easily gaining remote code execution.
* Unwanted Extension check now also runs on completed downloads.
* Changed the internal web framework from CherryPy to Starlette.
* Overview of Active Sessions is available when username and password are enabled.
* Updated the RSS overview page and added an option to download duplicate feed items,
  for RSS feeds (like indexer carts) that only remove items once they are fetched.
* Proxied requests are only allowed from hosts configured in `xff_trusted_hosts`.
  This prevents requests through a reverse proxy from being trusted as local.
* Template folder can no longer be configured manually, preventing abuse.
* Several settings no longer require a restart after changing them.
* Removed unused fields `completeness`, `meta`, `series`, `id`, and
  `script_log` from the `history` API response. The `script_log` of a completed
  download is now only available through the `scriptlog` API call.
* Cached `Public IPv4 address` for 10 minutes to prevent abuse.
* Windows/macOS: Updated Python to 3.15.2 and 7-Zip to 26.06.
* Snap: Several build and runtime improvements.

## Bug fixes in 5.2.0

* Downloads with `Repair` priority would not always be at the top of the queue.
* Failure to read one RSS URL would stop the whole readout instead of continuing to the next.
* Prevent potential XSS in the History from malicious Script output (GHSA-rpwc-qfxm-7h2v)
  or malicious NNTP responses (GHSA-c5x2-896f-g5g8).
* Download names that look like URLs could escape the Download folder (GHSA-73q2-vw82-jr46).
* Sorting allowed writing outside the Complete Directory through malicious metadata (GHSA-727m-c877-c8gf).
* Correct `articles_success` to `articles_failed` in Server statistics API call.
* Downloads could stall in case of unexpected server responses.
* Remove empty folders left behind by deleted samples.
* Stalled Unrar could freeze the post-processing queue.
* File handles could remain open after a download completed.
* Correctly handle `HEAD` responses during availability checks.
* Deobfuscation of some sets of RAR files would be skipped.
* Quota exceeded responses from news servers would be misinterpreted.
* Downloads with missing articles and no par2 would not be marked as failed.
* macOS: Tray icon would not show on macOS 27.
* macOS: Downloads could be unpacked twice due to different Unicode handling.

## Upgrade notices

* Python 3.10 support will be dropped in SABnzbd 5.3.
* You can directly upgrade from version 3.0.0 and newer.
* Upgrading from older versions will require performing a `Queue repair`.

## Code Signing Policy

Windows code signing is provided by SignPath.io using a SignPath Foundation certificate.

## About

SABnzbd is an open-source cross-platform binary newsreader.
It simplifies the process of downloading from Usenet dramatically, thanks to its web-based
user interface and advanced built-in post-processing options that automatically verify, repair,
extract and clean up posts downloaded from Usenet.

